      en: "The STAR Brewery (Société Tananarivienne d'Articles Réfrigérés) in Antananarivo is the flagship facility of Madagascar's dominant beverage company. Founded in 1953, STAR is deeply woven into the country's cultural and economic fabric, primarily known for producing THB (Three Horses Beer), the ubiquitous national beer. The Antananarivo plant is a massive industrial complex that produces millions of hectoliters of beer and soft drinks annually, including locally bottled Coca-Cola products. As one of the largest private employers and taxpayers in Madagascar, the brewery is a cornerstone of the manufacturing sector. The facility utilizes significant local agricultural inputs, particularly maize sourced from the Vakinankaratra region, linking industrial output with domestic farming. Geografi K6 — manufacturing industries and domestic consumption."
