      en: "La Cotonnière d'Antsirabe (Cotona) is one of the largest and most historic textile manufacturing plants in Madagascar. Established in the mid-20th century in Antsirabe, the factory is a massive integrated complex that handles everything from spinning raw cotton to weaving and dyeing the final fabric. Cotona has been a pillar of the local economy for decades, employing thousands of workers and significantly contributing to the nation's textile exports, which are heavily oriented toward European and American markets under favorable trade agreements like AGOA (African Growth and Opportunity Act). The facility's location in the highlands provides an optimal climate for textile production and easy access to the labor market of the Vakinankaratra region. Geografi K7 — textile manufacturing and international trade agreements."
